I've added an everyman role called "being." In other words, you are a
"lawful male human being."

* Race, sex, and alignment are unrestricted by the role; racial
restrictions still apply.
* Starting minimum stats are all level (at 7) with equal probabilities
for increase - this gives starting stats of around 13, with some
variation.
* The starting inventory is a knife.
* All skills are unrestricted, to a max of Skilled.
* The player starts with *no* skill, not even the knife.
* Magic skill and armor penalties are middle of the road.
* HP gain is middle of the road.
* The special spell is "polymorph." Heh.

It's kind of a weird feeling wandering around in the dungeon the first
few levels realizing that the first few items you pick up will
probably have a lasting effect on your gameplay, because they are
likely to be the weapons/spells you specialize in.

I am thinking that a good quest enemy might be "The Man," ("The Man
whips you! The Man kicks you! The Man crushes your spirit! The Man
gets you down!") deep in a building full of Kops and soldiers and
watchmen (and clerks and bureaucrats). The quest artifact ought to be
something that allows "plain old guy" to finally hit a groove. Perhaps
it could allow (or grant) Expert skill in one or more areas of the
player's choice. I'd have to think about how that might affect other
roles wishing for that same artifact. Or perhaps the artifact would be
something more mundane, and the end of the quest would leave the
player in a room stocked with all manner of armor, weapons, and
magical gear.

Anyway, other stuff is coming along.



